What this module does guarantee:

* it never raises anything but ValueError with a human-readable message
  (no tracebacks leaking to the assistant);
* every error names the problem AND offers a ready-to-run replacement;
* it accepts the obvious spelling of a field or operator as well as the
  official one, so a reasonable first guess works;
* string comparisons are case-insensitive and type-aware, because the worst
  outcome in this system is a silent "0 results" that the assistant reports
  as "there are none".
